We are pleased to announce that the Acheson Maritime River Cam has been
moved to the top of the City Municipal Office Building and is back in
operation.  Although shipping season is nearly over for the winter, save

a tug or a tanker now and then, there is plenty to see from the grand
and scenic vantage the camera now offers.  A vessel can be kept in view
for twenty-five minutes compared to just seven minutes of viewing from
the previous location.  On a clear day the camera can "see" out into
Lake Huron for at least ten miles.

The River Cam images can be seen at www.jclary.com, Cap'n Jim's Gallery,

The Bank One lobby at 600 Fort Street, and the Standard Station at the
corner of Military and Griswold Ave., in Port Huron, Michigan.

We are also working with COMCAST for the camera images
to be broadcast on local cable TV as well.

